{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01674",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.87,
      "end_seconds": 3.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.14,
      "end_seconds": 14.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 18.95,
      "end_seconds": 25.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Hello, um, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.79,
      "end_seconds": 28.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "absolutely, come and sit beside them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 30.38,
      "end_seconds": 36.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "we came because of pain under my right ribs after fatty meals"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.85,
      "end_seconds": 40.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Alright, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.36,
      "end_seconds": 49.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "About... well, two months. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.72,
      "end_seconds": 63.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.13,
      "end_seconds": 72.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "I'd say moderate. Honestly, all the time. Fatty meals definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.01,
      "end_seconds": 80.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "I, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 80.46,
      "end_seconds": 86.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.69,
      "end_seconds": 90.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "later, thanks please go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.8,
      "end_seconds": 93.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I've also been feeling sick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.51,
      "end_seconds": 106.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.53,
      "end_seconds": 112.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "It feels severe to me. I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.05,
      "end_seconds": 116.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Did you get dark urine or pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.3,
      "end_seconds": 128.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "no, no dark urine, no pale stools i did have bloating at one point, but that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.68,
      "end_seconds": 133.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Okay, did you get yellow eyes or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.48,
      "end_seconds": 137.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.76,
      "end_seconds": 141.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.08,
      "end_seconds": 148.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.73,
      "end_seconds": 151.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "okay, has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.96,
      "end_seconds": 153.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.97,
      "end_seconds": 172.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.83,
      "end_seconds": 175.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.75,
      "end_seconds": 184.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list? Bear with me, I'm just building up the the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.32,
      "end_seconds": 193.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.63,
      "end_seconds": 198.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.42,
      "end_seconds": 216.37,
      "duration_seconds": 15.95,
      "text": "for the stent, I believe my wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given i'm on something called an a... an antacid, 10 ml, maybe, when needed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.97,
      "end_seconds": 222.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.16,
      "end_seconds": 229.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "no, it's at home. Carbamazepine I don't take anymore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.97,
      "end_seconds": 233.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.04,
      "end_seconds": 249.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "I've had heart disease, yes. Epilepsy, for nearly five years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.97,
      "end_seconds": 251.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.04,
      "end_seconds": 261.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux for nearly five years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.61,
      "end_seconds": 267.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Okay, I can see acid reflux in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.18,
      "end_seconds": 285.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.7,
      "end_seconds": 296.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I swim twice a week. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 297.85,
      "end_seconds": 306.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 123 over 75, pulse is 80 beats a minute, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.63,
      "end_seconds": 308.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.43,
      "end_seconds": 313.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Let's move on to to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.74,
      "end_seconds": 315.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.77,
      "end_seconds": 318.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.83,
      "end_seconds": 333.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "It is tender under the right ribs and you stop breathing in when I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.36,
      "end_seconds": 352.16,
      "duration_seconds": 14.8,
      "text": "Please sit back down. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with gallstone-related pain at this stage. It could also be a stomach ulcer, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.84,
      "end_seconds": 355.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.53,
      "end_seconds": 376.33,
      "duration_seconds": 19.8,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with gallstone-related pain do well once it's treated properly. Let's get an ultrasound of the abdomen, for biliary pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's get liver blood tests, for biliary pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.79,
      "end_seconds": 382.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "let me think, when would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.68,
      "end_seconds": 408.83,
      "duration_seconds": 25.15,
      "text": "for this, paracetamol, 1 gram, four times a day when needed, one week it's for pain avoid fatty and fried foods until the scan we'll refer you to the surgical clinic and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.48,
      "end_seconds": 411.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.62,
      "end_seconds": 418.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.24,
      "end_seconds": 423.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.78,
      "end_seconds": 432.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "I'd like you back after the scan. Alright, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.96,
      "end_seconds": 437.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.52,
      "end_seconds": 444.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}